docs/adr/0008-workspace-layout-and-toolchain.md:35:**Answer entry (measured in the answer-page prototype, 2026-11-07).** The answer entry is prerendered static HTML with inline CSS and a small plain TypeScript controller, with no React, Preact, or Base UI. Measured with Lighthouse mobile (slow 4G, 4× CPU), the time until the Question text appears was 1.12 s with this approach, 1.35 s with Preact, 1.61 s with React, and 1.90 s with React plus Base UI. The token request starts from an inline script in `<head>`, and Effect Schema (23.5 KB gzip) loads after first paint. Budget: JS ≤ 10 KB gzip on the critical path, CSS ≤ 2 KB inline, HTML ≤ 8 KB, 1 request before first paint and 2 before the Question text. A Lighthouse CI gate checks FCP ≤ 800 ms, LCP ≤ 1.3 s, and TBT ≤ 50 ms.
docs/adr/0011-app-entry-uses-foldkit.md:5:- **App entry.** Foldkit and `@foldkit/ui` with Foldkit's typed bidirectional router. State is an Effect Schema Model with Messages, a pure `update`, `Command.define`, and a declarative `view`. React, react-dom, and `@base-ui/react` are removed from `apps/web`; React stays only in `packages/emails`. Tailwind v4 and the CSS custom property tokens stay. `foldkit`, `@foldkit/ui`, and `@foldkit/vite-plugin` are exact catalog pins that move together with the Effect pins.
